    hero: {
      title: 'SPOT HEARTS',
      subtitle: 'Card Game',
    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Spot Hearts',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Spot Hearts is a trick-taking variant where each heart scores its pip value (2 through 10 face value, jack 11, queen 12, king 13, ace 14; queen of spades 25). Players avoid winning tricks containing penalty cards; the game is played to a higher target (e.g. 500) and the lowest score wins.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Spot Hearts is a scoring variant of Hearts. Hearts first appeared at the end of the nineteenth century and is now popular in various forms in many countries; Spot Hearts keeps the standard American Hearts deal and play but assigns penalty points by each heart's pip value and a higher game target.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Four players. Spot Hearts is most commonly played by four; there are no formal partnerships.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'A standard 52-card deck is used, with no jokers. All 52 cards are dealt out one at a time so each player receives 13 cards. Spot Hearts uses the same deck as standard Hearts; only the penalty scoring differs (hearts count their pip value, queen of spades 25).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'A standard 52-card deck is used, with no jokers. All 52 cards are dealt out one at a time so each player receives 13 cards. Spot Hearts uses the same deck as standard Hearts; only the penalty scoring differs (hearts count their pip value, queen of spades 25).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal and play are clockwise. All 52 cards are dealt out one at a time so that each player has 13. After the deal, each player passes three cards face-down (first hand to the left, second to the right, third across, fourth hand no pass; the cycle repeats).',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
