      equipment: 'A standard 52-card deck is used, with no jokers. All 52 cards are dealt out one at a time so each player receives 13 cards. Spot Hearts uses the same deck as standard Hearts; only the penalty scoring differs (hearts count their pip value, queen of spades 25).',
      dealing: 'Deal and play are clockwise. All 52 cards are dealt out one at a time so that each player has 13. After the deal, each player passes three cards face-down (first hand to the left, second to the right, third across, fourth hand no pass; the cycle repeats).',
